ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-19T14:26:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-19T14:31:59Z","body":"> I believe a bug I reported could be related, since it shared a lot of the same symptoms: [#111695](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111695)\n\nYes it's related to all the `Control` nodes that updates it's own minimum size when width or height changes. <s>I wonder if it's an editor only issue related to CIE or it also crashes the exported game.</s>\n\nEdit: It also happens for exported game, will try to track the issue and fix it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419709237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532222539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108407#issuecomment-3532222539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108407","id":3532222539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SiXBL","user":{"login":"Reneator","id":24807557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODA3NTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24807557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator","html_url":"https://github.com/Reneator","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T11:06:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T11:06:56Z","body":"i have the same issue,\ninterestingly:\n\n<img width=\"1134\" height=\"641\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac0b5667-fbd2-4df2-8968-c5093362ba3f\" />\n\nThe running game only crashes if i started the editor it runs in, with the open console.\nIf I start the game inside an editor without the console, it takes the game like 18 seconds to render the elements and in the profiler its shown as \"18000ms physics time\".\n\nAlso this only happens in a specific ui element i have, in a different one it works without a hitch.\n\nIn combination with the othere infos here regarding min-size it might be some kind of a loop in a specific control-ui scenario:\n\nThis one creates the problem:\n\n<img width=\"1898\" height=\"959\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0af26360-5e6a-4d38-8cb1-2bdaae40b641\" />\n\nThis one works just fine:\n\n<img width=\"1894\" height=\"943\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86201d9f-2742-480a-9495-de06db4e5cdc\" />\n\nSo i imagine it could originate from the other Elements/the general treestructure above it.\n\nFor the problem scene, if i set a min-size for the direct parent-element, it still triggers the problem.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"u