"2025-11-17T16:56:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T16:58:02Z","body":"Checked as well with v4.6.dev4.official [bd2ca13c6] and the layout no longer goes wonky when editing min-sizes and the editor doesnt stutter/crash anymore:\n\nTo show the layout seems to properly work now.\n<img width=\"1902\" height=\"1014\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a11b737c-eb6b-439d-839c-75c54e72209f\" />\n\nTo show the hbox now properly encompasses the textureRect with the \"fit width\".\n<img width=\"1899\" height=\"956\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/beb2ecbd-7185-48f6-9af9-38f076ff7b14\" />\n\nExperimented a bit with min-size etc. and now it works properly with the MRP provided by OP\n\nThe project now properly starts up with no issues.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3542924948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544219956","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108407#issuecomment-3544219956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108407","id":3544219956,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TQIE0","user":{"login":"gkwaerp","id":35116814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTE2ODE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35116814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp","html_url":"https://github.com/gkwaerp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkwaerp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T23:05:54Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T23:05:54Z","body":"> I believe a bug I reported could be related, since it shared a lot of the same symptoms: [#111695](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111695)\n\nThis issue/MRP is **not** fixed in v4.6.dev4.official [bd2ca13c6].","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544219956/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3549107462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108407#issuecomment-3549107462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108407","id":3549107462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TixUG","user":{"login":"Reneator","id":24807557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODA3NTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24807557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator","html_url":"https://github.com/Reneator","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Reneator/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T18:54:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T19:49:26Z","body":"> > I believe a bug I reported could be related, since it shared a lot of the same symptoms: [#111695](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111695)\n> \n> This issue/MRP is **not** fixed in v4.6.dev4.official [[bd2ca13](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/bd2ca13c6f3a5198eac035c855dcd1759e077313)].\n\n\nMight be best to also mention this in the Ticket as well, if the info is only posted here it might get lost, because the Ticket already has a solution branch set.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3549107462/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4583231427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108407#issuecomment-4583231427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108407","id":4583231427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABES6Pww","user":{"login":"scrusi","id":137942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzk0Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi","html_url":"https://github.com/scrusi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scrusi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T15:17:58Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T15:17:58Z","body":"I ran into this (or a very similar) issue on 4.6.1-stable (built from 14d1969) and want to add a wrinkle that isn't really about the resizing itself, but about the \"Object was deleted while awaiting a callback\" messages. They aren't from the layout code but printed by by CallQueue::statistics(), which it seems the engine runs when it reports \"Message queue out of memory.\" So once the resize loop overflows the queue, the OOM-reporting path itself both spams those lines and then segfaults (it dereferences a callable in a Message that flush() already destructed). I think there might be a more general bug hiding behind the resize one: overflowing the queue during a flush crashes in the error-reporting path instead of failing cleanly. AI summary below:\n\nA symbolized dev build shows the actual crash is in the out-of-memory diagnostics path, not the layout code:\n\n```[0] Callable::get_object        core/variant/callable.cpp:164\n[1] CallQueue::statistics       core/object/message_queue.cpp:370\n[2] CallQueue::push_callablep   core/object/message_queue.cpp:98   (\"Message queue out of memory\")\n[10] CallQueue::_call_function  core/object/message_queue.cpp:220\n[11] CallQueue::flush           core/object/message_queue.cpp:268\n```\nflush() destructs each Message in place as it advances (message_queue.cpp:291) and re-reads pages_used each iteration (:245), so a call pushed during the flush is processed in the same flush. When such a push hits max_pages, push_callablep() calls statistics() (:98), which walks the entire queue — including the Messages flush already destructed — and dereferences freed callable data at callable.cpp:164.\n\nThis means the overflow-during-flush crash is independent of the specific container loop that fills the queue. Minimal repro (headless, no UI), crashes immediately with the stack above:\n\n```extends Node\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tcall_deferred(\"_bomb\")\nfunc _bomb() -> void:\n\tcall_deferred(\"_bomb\")\n\tcall_deferred(\"_bomb\")\n```\nIn our real case the queue was filled by a ScrollContainer (default SCROLL_MODE_AUTO) whose scrollbar-gutter visibility oscillated the content width during interaction churn; vertical_scroll_mode = SCROLL_MODE_RESERVE is an effective app-side workaround for that flavor.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4583231427/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]